      "message": "FWIW I also can\u0027t repro with my `args.gn`... :-(\n\nI wonder if the main thing that changed is that after this CL Bazel builds (triggered from `BUILD.gn`) started to also compile some core Skia C++.  Before this CL, Bazel builds would compile `libcxx_cc.a`, but other than that no C++ would be built via Bazel (when launched from `BUILD.gn`).  From this perspective, maybe `.rs` files should only depend on declarations and abstract interfaces (e.g. [the old `ReadAndSeekTraits`](https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1093916/23/rust/png/FFI.h) C++ class was a pure-virtual/abstract interface).\n\nI am sorry that I don\u0027t have any better or more concrete ideas... :-/",
