      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T01:34:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@kjlubick / @bungeman - do you think this is something that can be fixed forward?  CQ is clean so things seem to be in reasonably good shape.  But if other Skia developers are impacted/blocked by any of these issues, then maybe we should consider reverting?\n\n-------------------\n\nI hope that we can fix the build issues within the current build framework.  But at the same time I feel that having a build that straddles GN/ninja and Bazel is one of the root causes for the complexity and fragility of the build.  So I was wondering whether using a unified build system may be possible in the medium-term future.  When this was discussed a year ago [1] it seemed there were no good short-term alternatives, but back then:\n\n* Having a Bazel-only build seemed within reach.  Is removing `BUILD.gn` and having a Bazel-only CQ and dev-workflow still a long-term goal for Skia?\n* AFAIK GN/ninja-only C++-and-Rust was rejected, because 1) it would require tweaking Skia\u0027s `gn2bp` tool to ignore Rust targets and 2) there was a high-level, non-specific concern that some clients may be unable to depend on `gclient` and Chromium.  Maybe this is something we could revisit?\n\n[1] https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gWRQCziaIuVtZmussVpBR_cauhkMlYmBy54om_hwbZU/edit?usp\u003dsharing",
      "revId": "5c34096c48139dc40baef6b9d3132660105ef96c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
